Verdict: MAJOR
Findings:
- [major] Scorecard negative-authority guard is still only enforced on the contract, not the checklist — In `Pseudocode`, the plan says `contract/checklist must include "MUST NOT treat any tier-1 indexing scorecard under docs/reports/ as required canonical authority"`, but `validate_contract_docs()`, `TDD Test List -> test_tier1_contract_forbids_scorecard_as_required_canonical_authority`, and `Acceptance Criteria` only require that sentence in `docs/standards/TIER1_INDEXING_AND_CODE_PLACEMENT_CONTRACT.md`. That leaves `docs/standards/TIER1_INDEXING_CHECKLIST.md` unguarded, so blocker 4 is not fully closed.
- [minor] TDD is named but not operationalized as a required sequence — Workspace instructions require `TDD mandatory — tests before implementation`, but this plan only lists tests in `TDD Test List` and required passing commands in `Acceptance Criteria`. There is no plan step, pseudocode step, or acceptance criterion requiring `tests/docs/test_tier1_indexing_contract.py` to be written and exercised before editing `docs/standards/TIER1_INDEXING_AND_CODE_PLACEMENT_CONTRACT.md` and `docs/standards/TIER1_INDEXING_CHECKLIST.md`.
- [minor] Checklist repo scope is still under-evidenced against the cited baseline standard — `Acceptance Criteria` and `test_tier1_checklist_covers_all_scope_repos` require only `workspace-hub`, `digitalmodel`, `assetutilities`, and `aceengineer-website`, but the same plan’s `Resource Intelligence Summary -> Line excerpts` quotes `FILE_STRUCTURE_TAXONOMY.md` with a different starter-repo set. The draft does not cite a specific artifact or section that establishes why `worldenergydata`/`assethold` are out of scope while `workspace-hub`/`aceengineer-website` are in scope.

Checks performed:
- Checked the submitted draft’s `Deliverable`, `Pseudocode`, `TDD Test List`, `Acceptance Criteria`, and `Risks and Open Questions` for the six rerun focus items.
- Verified that the bulk-artifact-store rule is now concretized and that `/mnt/ace/data` is described as an example, not the universal rule.
- Verified that the daily freshness section now includes cadence wording plus an actual obligation to refresh/regenerate `docs/reports/tier-1-indexing-freshness-latest.md` and links `#2465`.
- Verified that checklist field names and allowed values are concrete.
- Checked for remaining internal contradictions between claimed rules and what the tests/acceptance criteria actually enforce; the unresolved contradiction is the scorecard negative-authority guard not being enforced on the checklist.
